/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
# `.conway/` holds BOTH generated state and deliberately-tracked project
# configuration, so this is an allowlist rather than a denylist: ignore
# everything, then re-admit the files a team is meant to share.
#
# It is written this way because the denylist form failed. It named the
# generated directories individually (`sessions/`, `paths/`), and when the
# path store's directory was derived from a renamed session root it became
# `<root>-paths` — the pattern silently stopped matching and test runs left
# content-addressed blobs in seven crate directories with nothing to announce
# it. An allowlist ignores a newly-invented generated directory by default;
# a denylist tracks it by default. Board item 01M0QK9GRM8HSNWRAR414TCX42.
**/.conway/*
!**/.conway/permissions.json
!**/.conway/settings.json
!**/.conway/agents/
!**/.conway/instructions.md

# ideate metadata — local-only tooling state (not tracked)
.ideate/
.ideate.json
.ideate-work/
.ideate-telemetry/

# Python bytecode caches. The six-gate script runs three Python checkers on
# every invocation, which regenerates these; tracking them means every worker
# tree reports itself dirty after running its own gates, and in a parallel
# worktree wave a dirty tree is the signal used to tell a stuck writer from a
# finished one. Ignore the cache, not the checkers.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
